@* ProductDetail.razor — Phase 3.2

   Customer-facing product detail page at route `/Products/{Id:guid}`.
   Reached from the Products grid (Phase 3.1) by clicking a product card.
   All authenticated users can view this page — it's the "shop window".

   LAYOUT (responsive):
     Desktop / tablet (≥768px): two columns
       Left  (5/12): product picture placeholder (square aspect ratio)
       Right (7/12): product info + purchase panel
     Mobile (<768px): single column, picture on top, info below

   SECTIONS (top to bottom on the right column):
     1. Breadcrumb: Products → [Category Name] → [Product Name]
        (Category Name is fetched via GetCategoryByIdWithHierarchyQuery;
        if the lookup fails for any reason, we just show "Products → [Name]"
        without the category — non-fatal.)
     2. Product name (h4)
     3. Price (large, primary color) + currency
     4. Stock badge: green "In stock (N)", orange "Low stock (N)",
        red "Out of stock"
     5. Description (paragraph, may wrap multiple lines)
     6. Purchase limits panel — ONLY shown to Admin/Manager (the
        GetProductByIdQuery handler strips purchase limits for other roles
        as a defense-in-depth measure). Lists per-group limits.
     7. Quantity selector (RadzenNumeric, min=1, max=StockQuantity)
     8. Add to Cart button — disabled if StockQuantity == 0 or while
        submitting. On success: success toast + clear quantity back to 1.

   DATA LOADING:
     - OnInitializedAsync: load the product via GetProductByIdQuery
       (Wolverine IMessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<ProductDto>>).
     - If the product loads successfully, fire a secondary query for the
       category (for the breadcrumb). The category load is non-fatal —
       if it fails, we just show "Products → [Product]" without the
       category crumb.

   ADD-TO-CART FLOW:
     - Dispatch CreateOrAppendSaleCommand(ProductId, Quantity) via
       Wolverine IMessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<Guid>>.
     - The handler:
         a. Loads the product (already loaded by the page, but the handler
            re-loads for atomicity — it's a separate scope).
         b. Finds the user's active Draft Sale (GetActiveDraftForUserAsync).
         c. Either creates a fresh draft with this line, or appends to the
            existing one. The Sale aggregate handles the increment-existing-
            line case (same ProductId on the sale) automatically.
         d. Returns Result<Guid> with the Sale Id.
     - On success: ToastService.Success with localized message, then reset
       quantity selector to 1. We DON'T navigate to /Cart (Phase 4.1 hasn't
       built that page yet — the user can keep browsing and add more items).
     - On failure: ToastService.Error with the result.Error message (the
       handler returns user-friendly messages like "Adding 5 units would
       bring your cart total to 15, but only 10 are currently in stock.").

   LOCALIZATION:
     All user-visible strings go through IStringLocalizer<ProductDetail> (Loc).
     Keys are defined in ProductDetail.fa-IR.resx (Persian, RTL) and
     ProductDetail.en-US.resx (English, LTR). RTL/LTR is handled at the
     <html dir="rtl"|"ltr"> level by MainLayout — individual pages don't
     need to do anything special.

   IMAGE STRATEGY:
     Phase 3.2 uses a PLACEHOLDER only — a Material icon (inventory_2)
     centered on a neutral background. The ProductDto has a PictureUrl
     field, but it's typically null in dev (no upload UI exists yet —
     Phase 7.1 will add one). If PictureUrl is set, we render an <img>;
     otherwise we show the placeholder. This keeps the page forward-
     compatible with future image support without us having to revisit
     it later.

   ANTI-FORGERY:
     Not needed — this page doesn't use EditForm. The Add to Cart button
     is a regular RadzenButton with a Click handler that calls into
     Wolverine. The Blazor circuit already has its anti-forgery token
     established at circuit-start time. No form POST happens.

   ROUTE PARAMETER:
     `Id` is a Guid bound from the URL via [Parameter]. Blazor's @page
     constraint `{Id:guid}` validates the URL segment is parseable as a
     Guid before this component even loads — a malformed URL gets a 404
     from the router, not a runtime exception here. *@

@page "/Products/{Id:guid}"
@attribute [Authorize]
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Interfaces
@using TakOne.Application.Products.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Queries.GetProductById
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Queries.GetCategoryByIdWithHierarchy
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Commands.CreateOrAppendSale
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.DTOs
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject ICurrentUserService CurrentUser
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<ProductDetail> Loc
@inject ToastService Toast

<PageTitle>@(_product is null ? Loc["PageTitle"] : $"{_product.Name} — TakOne")</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            /* Layout — 12-col grid on desktop/tablet, stacks on mobile */
            .detail-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
                gap: 2rem;
                align-items: start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 768px) {
                .detail-grid {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                    gap: 1.25rem;
                }
            }

            /* Picture — square aspect ratio, placeholder-friendly.
                                   We use the same neutral background + border as the Products grid
                                   card so the visual language is consistent across catalog + detail. */
            .detail-picture {
                aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-base-border-color);
                border-radius: var(--rz-border-radius);
                overflow: hidden;
                max-width: 480px;
            }

                .detail-picture img {
                    width: 100%;
                    height: 100%;
                    object-fit: contain;
                }

                .detail-picture .rz-icon {
                    font-size: 8rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                }

            /* Purchase panel — the right column */
            .detail-info {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 1rem;
            }

            .detail-name {
                font-size: 1.6rem;
                font-weight: 700;
                margin: 0;
                line-height: 1.2;
            }

            .detail-price {
                font-size: 1.75rem;
                font-weight: 700;
                color: var(--rz-primary);
                line-height: 1;
            }

            .detail-description {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                line-height: 1.6;
                white-space: pre-wrap; /* preserves newlines in description */
            }

            .stock-badge {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem;
                border-radius: 9999px;
                font-size: 0.85rem;
                font-weight: 600;
            }

            .stock-in {
                background: rgba(76, 175, 80, 0.15);
                color: #4caf50;
            }

            .stock-low {
                background: rgba(255, 152, 0, 0.15);
                color: #ff9800;
            }

            .stock-out {
                background: rgba(244, 67, 54, 0.15);
                color: #f44336;
            }

            /* Purchase limits panel — only admin/manager see this. */
            .limits-panel {
                border: 1px dashed var(--rz-base-border-color);
                border-radius: var(--rz-border-radius);
                padding: 1rem;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
            }

            .limits-list {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                margin: 0;
                padding: 0;
                list-style: none;
            }

                .limits-list li {
                    display: flex;
                    justify-content: space-between;
                    font-size: 0.9rem;
                }

                .limits-list .group-name {
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                }

                .limits-list .limit-value {
                    font-weight: 600;
                }

            /* Quantity selector + Add-to-cart button row */
            .purchase-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                align-items: stretch;
                margin-top: 0.5rem;
            }

                .purchase-row .qty-input {
                    width: 100px;
                }

                .purchase-row .add-to-cart-btn {
                    flex: 1;
                }

            @@media (max-width: 480px) {
                .purchase-row {
                    flex-direction: column;
                }

                    .purchase-row .qty-input {
                        width: 100%;
                    }
            }

            /* Breadcrumb */
            .breadcrumb {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                font-size: 0.85rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

                .breadcrumb a {
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    text-decoration: none;
                }

                    .breadcrumb a:hover {
                        color: var(--rz-primary);
                        text-decoration: underline;
                    }

                .breadcrumb .crumb-current {
                    color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                    font-weight: 600;
                }

                .breadcrumb .crumb-sep {
                    opacity: 0.5;
                }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Back button ──
       Always visible. Returns to /Products (preserves any ?category=... filter
       the user had set there if they use browser back, but we use NavigateTo
       so the back-stack stays clean). *@
    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BackToCatalog"]"
                  Icon="arrow_back"
                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                  Variant="Variant.Text"
                  Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Products", forceLoad: false))" />

    @* ── Loading state ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenCard>
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
                <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Medium" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["Loading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Error state ── *@
    else if (_loadError is not null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true" />
    }

    @* ── Not found ── *@
    else if (_product is null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["NotFoundTitle"]"
                     Text="@Loc["NotFoundMessage"]"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Warning"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true" />
    }

    @* ── Main content ── *@
    else
    {
        <div class="detail-grid">
            @* LEFT — picture (or placeholder) *@
            <div class="detail-picture">
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_product.PictureUrl))
                {
                    <img src="@_product.PictureUrl" alt="@_product.Name" loading="lazy" />
                }
                else
                {
                    <RadzenIcon Icon="inventory_2" />
                }
            </div>

            @* RIGHT — info + purchase panel *@
            <div class="detail-info">
                @* Breadcrumb: Products → [Category Name] → [Product Name] *@
                <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="breadcrumb">
                    <a href="/Products">@Loc["BreadcrumbProducts"]</a>
                    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_categoryName))
                    {
                        <span class="crumb-sep">/</span>
                        <span>@_categoryName</span>
                    }
                    <span class="crumb-sep">/</span>
                    <span class="crumb-current">@_product.Name</span>
                </nav>

                @* Product name *@
                <h1 class="detail-name">@_product.Name</h1>

                @* Price *@
                <div class="detail-price">@FormatPrice(_product.Price)</div>

                @* Stock badge *@
                @if (_product.StockQuantity == 0)
                {
                    <span class="stock-badge stock-out">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="error_outline" />
                        @Loc["StockOut"]
                    </span>
                }
                else if (_product.StockQuantity <= 10)
                {
                    <span class="stock-badge stock-low">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="warning_amber" />
                        @string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["StockLow"], _product.StockQuantity)
                    </span>
                }
                else
                {
                    <span class="stock-badge stock-in">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="check_circle" />
                        @string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["StockIn"], _product.StockQuantity)
                    </span>
                }

                @* Description *@
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_product.Description))
                {
                    <p class="detail-description">@_product.Description</p>
                }

                @* Purchase limits panel — admin/manager only.
                   The handler already strips limits for other roles, so the
                   PurchaseLimits collection will be empty for customers.
                   We additionally gate the UI on role check for clarity. *@
                @if (_product.PurchaseLimits.Count > 0
                     && (CurrentUser.IsInRole(Roles.Admin) || CurrentUser.IsInRole(Roles.Manager)))
                {
                    <div class="limits-panel">
                        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem" Style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="rule" />
                            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["PurchaseLimitsTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
                        </RadzenStack>
                        <ul class="limits-list">
                            @foreach (var limit in _product.PurchaseLimits)
                            {
                                <li>
                                    <span class="group-name">@limit.GroupName</span>
                                    <span class="limit-value">@string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["PurchaseLimitValue"], limit.Limit)</span>
                                </li>
                            }
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                }

                @* Purchase panel: quantity selector + Add to cart button.
                   Disabled if out of stock OR currently submitting. *@
                <div class="purchase-row">
                    <RadzenNumeric @bind-Value="_quantity"
                                   Min="1"
                                   Max="@_product.StockQuantity"
                                   Step="1"
                                   Style="width: 100px;"
                                   class="qty-input"
                                   Disabled="@(_product.StockQuantity == 0 || _isSubmitting)" />
                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["AddToCart"]"
                                  Icon="add_shopping_cart"
                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                  Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                  class="add-to-cart-btn"
                                  Disabled="@(_product.StockQuantity == 0 || _isSubmitting)"
                                  Click="@HandleAddToCartAsync" />
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── Route parameter ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Product Id from the URL. The @page constraint `{Id:guid}` ensures
    /// only valid Guid strings reach this parameter; malformed URLs hit
    /// the router's NotFound template instead.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Guid Id { get; set; }

    // ── State ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private ProductDto? _product;
    private string? _categoryName;
    private string? _loadError;
    private bool _isLoading = true;
    private int _quantity = 1;
    private bool _isSubmitting;

    // ── Lifecycle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            await LoadProductAsync();
            // Fire-and-forget the category lookup — it's non-fatal. We
            // could parallelize, but the category lookup depends on
            // _product.CategoryId being populated, so it has to come
            // after the product load anyway.
            await LoadCategoryNameAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadProductAsync()
    {
        var query = new GetProductByIdQuery { ProductId = Id };
        var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<ProductDto>>(query);

        if (result.IsSuccess)
        {
            _product = result.Value;
        }
        else
        {
            // result.Error contains the handler's user-friendly message
            // (e.g. "Product '{Id}' was not found.")
            _loadError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
        }
    }

    private async Task LoadCategoryNameAsync()
    {
        if (_product is null || _product.CategoryId == Guid.Empty)
        {
            return;
        }

        try
        {
            var query = new GetCategoryByIdWithHierarchyQuery { CategoryId = _product.CategoryId };
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<CategoryDto>>(query);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                _categoryName = result.Value.Name;
            }
            // Non-fatal: if category fails to load, breadcrumb just shows
            // "Products / [Product]" without the category crumb.
        }
        catch
        {
            // Swallow — category is purely a UI nicety for the breadcrumb.
        }
    }

    // ── Add-to-cart ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task HandleAddToCartAsync()
    {
        if (_product is null || _quantity < 1)
        {
            return;
        }

        _isSubmitting = true;

        try
        {
            var command = new CreateOrAppendSaleCommand(_product.Id, _quantity);
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<Guid>>(command);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                // Success toast. We don't navigate to /Cart yet (Phase 4.1
                // will add that page) — the user can keep browsing.
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["AddedToCart"], _quantity, _product.Name),
                    summary: Loc["AddedToCartTitle"]);

                // Reset quantity back to 1 so the user can add a different
                // product (or the same one again) without first clearing
                // the field.
                _quantity = 1;
            }
            else
            {
                // result.Error contains a user-friendly message from the
                // handler (e.g. "Adding 5 units of 'Widget' would bring
                // your cart total to 15, but only 10 are currently in stock.")
                await Toast.Error(
                    result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericAdd"],
                    summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            // Defensive: any unexpected exception (Wolverine timeout, etc.)
            // gets a generic message. Don't leak exception details.
            await Toast.Error(
                Loc["Error_GenericAdd"],
                summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isSubmitting = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Display helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a MoneyDto for display. IRR is converted to Toman (amount ÷ 10)
    /// and labelled "تومان" — matches the Products grid convention so a
    /// customer sees the same unit on the listing and the detail page.
    /// Other currencies pass through unchanged.
    /// </summary>
    private static string FormatPrice(MoneyDto price)
    {
        if (price is null) return "—";
        var isIrr = string.Equals(price.Currency, "IRR", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        var displayAmount = isIrr ? price.Amount / 10m : price.Amount;
        var amount = displayAmount.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture);
        var unit = isIrr ? "تومان" : price.Currency;
        return $"{amount} {unit}";
    }
}